---
/*
  ============================================================
  FONT SPECIMEN — /lab/specimen/
  ============================================================
  Part of the /lab/ comparison set (see 04.08/lab-editing-map.md).
  Purpose: show Andrew's six candidate fonts against real copy —
  one font per block, each block a *different* block-type, size,
  and alignment (font-per-block, no repetition). The point is to
  stress-test, so the two techno faces (Oxanium, Nova Square) are
  handed real paragraphs, not just headlines, to show where a
  squared display face breaks down as sustained body text.

  This page is standalone: no BaseLayout, no global nav — it
  writes its own <html><head><body> shell so the neutral surface
  is the only constant and the fonts are the variable.

  FONT -> BLOCK-TYPE MAP (each unique):
    B1 premise       Roboto Flex        prose         (Stripe Press)
    B2 palette list  Ubuntu Condensed   rhythm-list   (Linear)
    B3 long-text     Cuprum             plain-cta     (37signals/Basecamp)
    B4 rhythm/stat   Space Mono         stat-dense    (Stripe)
    B5 bare imagery  JetBrains Mono*    bare-frame    (Stripe)  *adjacent family
    B6 warning       Oxanium            sidenote      (Works in Progress)
    B7 harvest close Nova Square        statement     (Stripe Press)

  *JetBrains Mono is the adjacent-family pick (technical-editing.md
   §2, Mono group) for the 7th presentable block. It carries the
   bare-frame doc-excerpt so Space Mono can appear on its own block
   (B4) while the mono doc-excerpt still reads as a monospace artifact.

  Type scale per §1: body >=18px; 16 and below only for notes/captions.
  Soft gradients per §3: focal blocks nudge darker, peripheral lighter,
  <=8% lightness delta, warm-white and orange whispers alternated.
  Captions per §4: every block closes with an italic, ~55%-opacity
  caption set in that block's own font, reporting the harvest string.
*/
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Font Specimen — /lab/</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />

  <!-- All specimen fonts loaded from Google Fonts. Astro hoists <link rel> into <head>. -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cuprum:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Nova+Square&family=Oxanium:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Roboto+Flex:opsz,wght@8..144,400;8..144,500&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Ubuntu+Condensed&display=swap"
  />

  <style is:global>
    :root {
      /* Neutral near-white specimen surface — the fonts, not a palette, are the variable. */
      --surface:        #FAFAF9;
      --surface-lift:   #FEFEFD; /* peripheral: recede toward light */
      --surface-deep:   #EFEEEA; /* focal: amplify toward near-black (warm), ~4-5% L delta */
      --surface-warm:   #F4EEE7; /* focal alt: orange-tinted whisper */
      --ink:            #23231F;
      --ink-soft:       #4A4944;
      --rule:           #E8E8E6;
      --accent:         #CC6A3C; /* brand-orange, used only as a whisper in gradients */
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html, body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--ink);
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    /* --- gradients (§3): a whisper, never harsh --- */
    .grad-recede { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface) 0%, var(--surface-lift) 100%); }
    .grad-focus  { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface-lift) 0%, var(--surface-deep) 100%); }
    .grad-focus-warm { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface-lift) 0%, var(--surface-warm) 100%); }

    /* --- shared block frame --- */
    .blk { padding: 5rem 1.5rem; }
    .col { max-width: 62ch; margin-inline: auto; }

    /* every block closes with a caption in its own font */
    .cap {
      margin-top: 2.25rem;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      opacity: 0.55;
    }
    .cap em { font-style: italic; }

    .page-head {
      max-width: 62ch;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 4rem 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
    .page-head h1 {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 22px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .page-head p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 15px;
      opacity: 0.55;
    }

    /* ---------- B1 prose (Roboto Flex) ---------- */
    .b1 p {
      font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      text-align: justify;
      hyphens: auto;
    }
    .b1 .cap { font-family: 'Roboto Flex', sans-serif; text-align: left; }

    /* ---------- B2 rhythm-list (Ubuntu Condensed) — Linear ---------- */
    .b2 * { font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif; }
    .b2 .eyebrow {
      font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: 0.4px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      opacity: 0.7;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .b2 h2 {
      font-size: 32px;
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      font-weight: 400;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .b2 .rhythm { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .b2 .rhythm li {
      padding-block: 0.9rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .b2 .rhythm b { font-weight: 700; }
    .b2 .cap { font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif; }

    /* ---------- B3 plain-cta (Cuprum) — 37signals / Basecamp ---------- */
    .b3 { text-align: center; }
    .b3 .col { max-width: 54ch; }
    .b3 h2 {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 26px;
      line-height: 1.25;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .b3 ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .b3 li {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-size: 22px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }
    .b3 li b { font-weight: 700; }
    .b3 .cta { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
    .b3 .btn {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--surface);
      background: var(--ink);
      text-decoration: none;
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 6px;
      display: inline-block;
    }
    .b3 .cap { font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif; }

    /* ---------- B4 stat-dense (Space Mono) — Stripe ---------- */
    .b4 { text-align: center; }
    .b4 .col { max-width: 48ch; }
    .b4 .stat {
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 2rem 1.75rem;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.4);
    }
    .b4 .fig {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .b4 .src {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .b4 .cav {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      opacity: 0.6;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b4 .cap { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; }

    /* ---------- B5 bare-frame (JetBrains Mono — adjacent) — Stripe ---------- */
    .b5 .col { max-width: 64ch; }
    .b5 .bare { margin: 0; }
    .b5 .doc-excerpt {
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      background: var(--surface-lift);
    }
    .b5 .doc-excerpt .anno {
      display: block;
      font-size: 15px;
      opacity: 0.6;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }
    .b5 .cap { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }

    /* ---------- B6 sidenote (Oxanium) — Works in Progress ---------- */
    .b6 .col { max-width: 78ch; }
    .b6 .wrap {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 62ch) 15rem;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }
    .b6 .body p {
      font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b6 .side {
      font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      opacity: 0.6;
      align-self: start;
    }
    .b6 .cap { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .b6 .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .b6 .side {
        border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
        padding-left: 1rem;
      }
    }

    /* ---------- B7 statement (Nova Square) — Stripe Press ---------- */
    .b7 { text-align: center; }
    .b7 .col { max-width: 40ch; }
    .b7 h2 {
      font-family: 'Nova Square', sans-serif;
      font-size: 40px;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.005em;
      margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    }
    .b7 .lede {
      font-family: 'Nova Square', sans-serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b7 .cap { font-family: 'Nova Square', sans-serif; }

    .foot {
      max-width: 62ch;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem 5rem;
      font-size: 15px;
      opacity: 0.5;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Font specimen — six candidates, one per block</h1>
    <p>/lab/ comparison set. Each block: a different font, size, block-type, and alignment. Techno faces carry real paragraphs on purpose.</p>
  </header>

  <!-- template: prose · treatment: Stripe Press -->
  <section class="blk b1 grad-focus">
    <div class="col">
      <p>Your premise holds. A live site is a better template source than a template marketplace, because you can read the decisions rather than inherit someone's content model. And the reskin is only about six variables: neutral ramp, one accent, radius scale, spacing scale, text measure, border weight. Fix those six and any layout you admire becomes yours.</p>
      <p class="cap"><em>Roboto Flex · 18/1.65 · 62ch · justified · 1px #E8E8E6 · r6 · 5rem:1.5rem — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: rhythm-list · treatment: Linear -->
  <section class="blk b2 grad-recede">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">Palette + surface</p>
      <h2>The white-main systems worth copying wholesale</h2>
      <ul class="rhythm">
        <li><b>Mercury</b> — the reference for premium-restrained off-white. Near-invisible borders, almost no shadow, one accent used sparingly. Serious without being cold, which is your construction-buyer problem exactly.</li>
        <li><b>Anthropic</b> — warm ivory ground, serif headings, very low saturation. Closest live example of your §1 brief: calm enough to read as a default rather than a pitch.</li>
        <li><b>Attio</b> — white, precise, tight grid. Shows how far a single accent goes when everything else is neutral.</li>
        <li><b>Notion</b> — the smoothed-edges reference. Radius scale, soft card fills, warm white. Study it for where rounding stops; over-rounding is what makes a premium site read as a toy.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cap"><em>Ubuntu Condensed · 32/1.15 head, 18/1.55 items · 62ch · left · top-rule 1px #E8E8E6 · r0 · 5rem:0.9rem — similar to Linear.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: plain-cta · treatment: 37signals / Basecamp -->
  <section class="blk b3 grad-recede">
    <div class="col">
      <h2>Long-text handling — you have a wordy site, so this matters more than palette</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Stripe Press</b> — book typography on the web. Measure control, no chrome, headings that hold their own without decoration.</li>
        <li><b>Works in Progress</b> — sidenotes, footnotes, sustained reading. Relevant to your Notion-docs layer and the sample teardowns.</li>
        <li><b>37signals / Basecamp</b> — plain speech, opinionated blocks, one CTA, active refusal of decoration. The nearest ethos match to your §6 and §9.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/varpage/teardown/">Request a free teardown →</a></div>
      <p class="cap"><em>Cuprum · 26/1.25 head, 22/1.6 items · 54ch · center · none · r6 · 5rem:1.25rem — similar to 37signals / Basecamp.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: stat-dense · treatment: Stripe -->
  <section class="blk b4 grad-focus-warm">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="stat">
        <p class="fig">Block rhythm and sequencing — big SaaS</p>
        <p class="src"><b>Linear</b> — take the spacing rhythm and the restraint, invert the palette. The lesson is vertical rhythm, and whitespace used structurally.</p>
        <p class="cav"><b>Stripe</b> — how to sequence dense information so density stops feeling heavy. Useful for your §5, where you have a statistic plus a source plus a caveat in one block.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="cap"><em>Space Mono · 28 fig / 18 src / 16 cav · 48ch · center · 1px #E8E8E6 · r8 · 4rem:1rem — similar to Stripe.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: bare-frame · treatment: Stripe -->
  <section class="blk b5 grad-recede">
    <div class="col">
      <figure class="bare">
        <div class="doc-excerpt">
          <span class="anno">// teardown-excerpt.md — bare frame, no device chrome</span>
          Mercury, Ramp, and Arc all show images without device frames, drop shadows, or perspective tilt. That is the current premium signal, and it happens to be the only image treatment that fits you.
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="cap"><em>JetBrains Mono (adjacent to Space Mono) · 18/1.55 · 64ch · left · 1px #E8E8E6 · r6 · 1.5rem padding — similar to Stripe (bare doc-excerpt).</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: sidenote · treatment: Works in Progress -->
  <section class="blk b6 grad-recede">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="body">
          <p>Every roundup this year says the same three things: put the product in motion at the top, add micro-interactions, consider dark mode. Two of those are wrong for you. You have no product UI to demo, and dark mode fights the calm-default frame you decided to install. Your equivalent of the interactive product moment is a real teardown excerpt rendered as a document — styled like a page from the artifact the client would receive, monospace annotations and all. That is your hero image and your §7 proof in one object.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="side">One warning about the 2026 consensus. Read this beside the body, not after it — the margin is where the caution belongs.</aside>
      </div>
      <p class="cap"><em>Oxanium · 18/1.6 body, 16 note · 62ch + 15rem margin · left · 2px #E8E8E6 left-rule (mobile) · r0 · 2.5rem gap — similar to Works in Progress.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- template: statement · treatment: Stripe Press -->
  <section class="blk b7 grad-focus">
    <div class="col">
      <h2>What to actually harvest</h2>
      <p class="lede">Open each of these, then write down only: the radius value, the body measure in characters, the border color and weight, the ratio between section padding and paragraph spacing, the type pairing. Five numbers and two fonts. That set, applied to any block library, gets you closer to a coherent site than any theme purchase will.</p>
      <p class="cap"><em>Nova Square · 40/1.1 head, 20/1.7 body · 40ch · center · none · r0 · 6rem:1.75rem — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="foot">Specimen only — no global nav, no shared layout. Neutral surface held constant so the font is the variable.</div>

</body>
</html>
